#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# lyapunov_solve

#% text
# `lyapunov_solve(a, c)` gives the matrix x with `a . x + x . conjugate_transpose(a) == c`.

#% text
# `lyapunov_solve(a, b, c)` gives the matrix x with `a . x + x . b == c` (the Sylvester equation).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The equation is solved as the linear system `(I (x) a + transpose(b) (x) I) vec(x) == vec(c)` with Kronecker products; exact matrices give exact solutions.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
lyapunov_solve([[1, 3], [2, 1]], [[-2, -1], [-1, -4]])
#% output
#= [[11/10, -7/10], [-7/10, -3/5]]

#% cell
lyapunov_solve([[-1, 1], [1, -2]], [[-1, 0], [0, 0]])
#% output
#= [[5/6, 1/3], [1/3, 1/6]]

#% cell
let a = [[-3, 2], [-1, -1]]
let x = lyapunov_solve(a, [[1, 0], [0, 1]])
dot(a, x) + dot(x, transpose(a))
#% output
#= [[1, 0], [0, 1]]

#% cell
lyapunov_solve([[1, 2], [0, 3]], [[2, 0], [1, 1]], [[1, 1], [1, 1]])
#% output
#= [[3/20, 1/4], [3/20, 1/4]]

